cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use IntentTrace in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "IntentTrace: A Reliability and Evaluation Framework for Hidden Information-Integrity Failures in Distributed Personalization Systems"
abstract: >-
  IntentTrace is an open, nonproprietary framework for detecting, reproducing,
  tracing, and benchmarking hidden information-integrity failures in
  personalization, recommendation, and AI-enabled distributed systems —
  failures in which every service reports healthy while the information
  driving the final decision is stale, missing, delayed, duplicated,
  conflicting, or misinterpreted.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Yellanki
    given-names: Srinivas Kalyan
repository-code: "https://github.com/syellanki09/intenttrace"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - software reliability
  - distributed systems
  - personalization
  - observability
  - data provenance
  - fault injection
  - reproducible benchmarks
